 Surface events (`user/message`, `assistant/message`, `tool/result`) must declare how they join the ordered surface; raw chunks, boundaries, and other log-only events never produce a message.
 
+An out-of-repository plugin may declaration-merge an informational, log-only event type and commit it with `session.appendIgnorable(type, data)`. The method accepts only event types absent from this build's generated known-event list, applies the same detached JSON snapshot and publication checks as `append()`, and stores `ignorable: true` so a harness without the plugin can reload the record without interpreting it. Known first-party events and every surface event must use `append()` ([decision](../../../.agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-08-30-retain-ignorable-external-session-events.md)).
+
 ### Read the log
 
 `session.seq` reads the current log length without materializing an array, and `session.eventAt(seq)` reads one accepted, deeply frozen event by sequence number. `session.snapshotEvents(fromSeq?, toSeqExclusive?)` materializes a frozen, stable snapshot of a half-open range; a complete current snapshot is cached until the next append. Callers that only need a length or one event use `seq` or `eventAt()`.
